1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
Setting up your machine.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:05,999
Before anything else.

3
00:00:05,999 --> 00:00:09,532
If you already have Python three twelve, git,

4
00:00:09,532 --> 00:00:14,399
and you know what a virtual environment is, skip this episode.

5
00:00:14,399 --> 00:00:16,519
Go straight to episode one.

6
00:00:16,519 --> 00:00:18,168
I will see you there.

7
00:00:18,968 --> 00:00:21,596
For everyone else, this is short.

8
00:00:21,596 --> 00:00:23,984
We are installing four things.

9
00:00:23,984 --> 00:00:30,434
Python three twelve, an editor, git, and we will get comfortable with a terminal.

10
00:00:31,234 --> 00:00:35,375
And just as importantly, what we are not installing.

11
00:00:35,375 --> 00:00:36,888
No database server.

12
00:00:36,888 --> 00:00:42,382
Episodes one to twelve use SQLite, which already ships inside Python.

13
00:00:42,382 --> 00:00:47,319
Postgres turns up in episode thirteen and we install it there.

14
00:00:47,319 --> 00:00:48,275
And no Node.

15
00:00:48,275 --> 00:00:53,212
There is no front end build step in this series, at any point.

16
00:00:54,012 --> 00:00:56,922
Step one, Python three point twelve.

17
00:00:56,922 --> 00:01:00,640
On Windows, use the installer from python.org.

18
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,014
On Mac, homebrew.

19
00:01:02,014 --> 00:01:08,642
On Debian or Ubuntu, apt &mdash; and note that the venv package is separate there.

20
00:01:08,642 --> 00:01:15,270
If you miss it, creating a virtual environment fails later with a confusing error.

21
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:22,323
Windows users, this one box causes more failed setups than everything else combined.

22
00:01:22,323 --> 00:01:27,237
On the first screen of the installer, tick add python.exe to path.

23
00:01:27,237 --> 00:01:32,894
If you already installed without it, run the installer again, choose modify,

24
00:01:32,894 --> 00:01:34,160
and tick it then.

25
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:36,319
Check it worked.

26
00:01:36,319 --> 00:01:39,887
On Windows, p y space minus minus version.

27
00:01:39,887 --> 00:01:44,219
On Mac and Linux, python three minus minus version.

28
00:01:44,219 --> 00:01:47,447
You want three point twelve something.

29
00:01:47,447 --> 00:01:52,714
If it says command not found on Windows, that is the path box.

30
00:01:53,514 --> 00:01:55,247
Step two, an editor.

31
00:01:55,247 --> 00:02:02,266
I use VS Code with the Python extension, and that is what you will see on screen.

32
00:02:02,266 --> 00:02:04,085
But any editor works.

33
00:02:04,085 --> 00:02:06,252
PyCharm, Neovim, Sublime.

34
00:02:06,252 --> 00:02:09,371
Do not spend an afternoon on themes.

35
00:02:09,371 --> 00:02:11,364
Install it and move on.

36
00:02:12,164 --> 00:02:13,482
Step three, git.

37
00:02:13,482 --> 00:02:19,084
Windows, use the installer from git-scm.com and accept the defaults.

38
00:02:19,084 --> 00:02:21,309
Mac and Linux, one command.

39
00:02:21,309 --> 00:02:23,451
Then tell git who you are.

40
00:02:23,451 --> 00:02:30,206
You need git because every episode of this series ends on a tag you can check out.

41
00:02:31,006 --> 00:02:34,127
Step four, and this is the one that matters.

42
00:02:34,127 --> 00:02:39,305
A virtual environment is just a folder that holds one project's packages.

43
00:02:39,305 --> 00:02:44,766
Without it, every Python project on your machine shares one set of libraries.

44
00:02:44,766 --> 00:02:49,305
Two projects that need different versions of Wagtail will fight,

45
00:02:49,305 --> 00:02:51,788
and you will lose an evening to it.

46
00:02:51,788 --> 00:02:53,632
With one, they never meet.

47
00:02:54,432 --> 00:02:55,507
Two commands.

48
00:02:55,507 --> 00:02:57,657
Make it, then activate it.

49
00:02:57,657 --> 00:03:02,618
On Mac and Linux the activate command is slightly different,

50
00:03:02,618 --> 00:03:04,602
and it is on screen now.

51
00:03:05,402 --> 00:03:07,072
Look at your prompt.

52
00:03:07,072 --> 00:03:10,161
It now starts with .venv in brackets.

53
00:03:10,161 --> 00:03:12,832
That prefix is the whole lesson.

54
00:03:12,832 --> 00:03:16,172
It means you are inside the environment.

55
00:03:16,972 --> 00:03:18,250
Here is the trap.

56
00:03:18,250 --> 00:03:23,588
Opening a new terminal window starts you outside the environment again.

57
00:03:23,588 --> 00:03:26,520
You have to activate every single time.

58
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:31,030
This is the number one reason that, three episodes from now,

59
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:33,962
a command suddenly cannot find Wagtail.

60
00:03:33,962 --> 00:03:35,015
Nothing broke.

61
00:03:35,015 --> 00:03:37,270
You are just outside the venv.

62
00:03:38,070 --> 00:03:39,843
One more Windows thing.

63
00:03:39,843 --> 00:03:45,086
If activate fails saying running scripts is disabled on this system,

64
00:03:45,086 --> 00:03:48,016
that is PowerShell's execution policy.

65
00:03:48,016 --> 00:03:52,102
Run the command on screen, answer yes, and try again.

66
00:03:52,102 --> 00:03:55,032
It only affects your own user account.

67
00:03:55,832 --> 00:03:59,453
Let us check everyone is in the same place.

68
00:03:59,453 --> 00:04:00,717
Three commands.

69
00:04:00,717 --> 00:04:03,243
Python, git, and venv support.

70
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:07,370
If all three run without an error, you are ready.

71
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:11,295
Notice we have not installed Wagtail at all.

72
00:04:11,295 --> 00:04:12,645
That is deliberate.

73
00:04:12,645 --> 00:04:15,415
It is the first command of episode one.

74
00:04:15,415 --> 00:04:21,381
Delete the practice folder, because the real project starts from an empty directory.

75
00:04:21,381 --> 00:04:27,063
And if anything failed, leave a comment with your operating system and the exact

76
00:04:27,063 --> 00:04:27,844
error text.

77
00:04:28,644 --> 00:04:35,599
Next episode, we install Wagtail, create a project, and log into a real CMS admin.

78
00:04:35,599 --> 00:04:40,518
And then we stop, and read every single file it generated.

79
00:04:41,318 --> 00:04:44,108
That is your starting line.

80
00:04:44,108 --> 00:04:47,518
Next episode, we install Wagtail.
